# Shared agent context

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first for the full playbook.

## Before code changes

1. Check `.agents/memory/MEMORY.md` and open any linked memory file relevant to the task.
2. If a project skill in `.agents/skills/` matches, **read that SKILL.md fully** before editing.
3. Respect `admin-web-stack.md` — no forbidden libraries, no hardcoded color values, no mock data.

## Skill triggers (mandatory)

| Task | Skill path |
|------|------------|
| Modifying any dashboard page | `.agents/skills/page-edit-safety/SKILL.md` |
| Adding Firestore queries or new API endpoints | `.agents/skills/firestore-integration/SKILL.md` |

## Cursor + Antigravity must stay aligned

- Shared truth lives in `.agents/memory/`, `.agents/skills/`, and `AGENTS.md`.
- Do not introduce parallel conventions that Antigravity would not follow.
- Do not modify `.replit` or Replit artifact configs unless explicitly requested.
- Keep edits focused; reuse existing Shadcn components from `artifacts/admin-web/src/components/ui/`.
